# Integration Events

## Purpose

This chapter defines the canonical events governing communication between Legacy and external systems.

Unlike Business Events, which represent authoritative League state, Integration Events describe the controlled exchange of information between Legacy and outside services.

These services may include:

- Fantasy platforms (Sleeper, ESPN, Yahoo)
- Authentication providers
- Payment providers
- Notification services
- Artificial Intelligence providers
- Public APIs
- Internal microservices
- Future third-party integrations

Integration Events never directly modify League state.

Every accepted external change must first become a validated Business Event.

---

# Guiding Principle

External systems provide information.

Legacy validates information.

Legacy creates Business Events.

Business Events change League state.

External systems are consumers and producers of messages—not owners of League state.

---

# Integration Model

```text
External System
        │
        ▼
Integration Event
        │
Validation
        │
        ▼
Command
        │
        ▼
Business Event
        │
        ▼
League State
```

Outgoing communication follows the reverse path.

```text
Business Event
        │
        ▼
Integration Event
        │
        ▼
External System
```

---

# Scope

This chapter defines:

- ExternalDataReceived
- ExternalSynchronizationStarted
- ExternalSynchronizationCompleted
- ExternalSynchronizationFailed

- AuthenticationSucceeded
- AuthenticationFailed

- NotificationQueued
- NotificationDelivered
- NotificationFailed

- PaymentReceived
- SubscriptionActivated
- SubscriptionCancelled

- AIRequestSubmitted
- AIResponseReceived
- AIResponseRejected

- WebhookReceived
- WebhookProcessed
- WebhookRejected

---

# General Invariants

Every Integration Event shall satisfy:

1. External systems never directly modify League state.
2. Every inbound message is validated.
3. Invalid messages are rejected.
4. Every accepted message produces deterministic Business Events.
5. Every outbound message references an existing Business Event.
6. Integration failures never corrupt League state.
7. External retries are idempotent.
8. Integration history is auditable.
9. Provider-specific payloads remain isolated.
10. League state is never dependent upon provider availability.

---

# ExternalDataReceived

## Purpose

Represents receipt of data from an external system.

Examples include:

- Sleeper roster updates
- Sleeper player metadata
- ESPN league imports
- Yahoo imports

### Business Impact

• Creates integration record

• Begins validation

• Does not modify League state

---

# ExternalSynchronizationStarted

## Purpose

Represents the beginning of an external synchronization operation.

### Business Impact

• Begins synchronization

• Creates synchronization transaction

• Tracks synchronization status

---

# ExternalSynchronizationCompleted

## Purpose

Represents successful completion of synchronization.

### Business Impact

• Updates synchronization history

• Enables downstream processing

• May emit Business Events

---

# ExternalSynchronizationFailed

## Purpose

Represents unsuccessful synchronization.

### Business Impact

• Preserves previous League state

• Records failure reason

• Enables retry

---

# AuthenticationSucceeded

## Purpose

Represents successful identity verification through an authentication provider.

Examples:

- Supabase Auth
- OAuth
- Email Login
- Passkeys

### Business Impact

• Authenticates User

• Enables session creation

• Does not modify League state

---

# AuthenticationFailed

## Purpose

Represents unsuccessful authentication.

### Business Impact

• Records failure

• Prevents unauthorized access

---

# NotificationQueued

## Purpose

Represents scheduling of an outbound notification.

Examples:

- Trade notification

- League invitation

- Waiver results

- Weekly recap

### Business Impact

• Creates delivery request

• Enables asynchronous delivery

---

# NotificationDelivered

## Purpose

Represents successful notification delivery.

### Business Impact

• Records delivery status

• Enables notification history

---

# NotificationFailed

## Purpose

Represents unsuccessful delivery.

### Business Impact

• Records failure

• Enables retry

---

# PaymentReceived

## Purpose

Represents successful receipt of payment.

Examples:

- League subscription

- Premium membership

- Marketplace purchase

### Business Impact

• Records financial transaction

• Enables subscription processing

• Does not directly activate features

---

# SubscriptionActivated

## Purpose

Represents activation of subscription benefits.

### Business Impact

• Grants product access

• Updates subscription state

---

# SubscriptionCancelled

## Purpose

Represents cancellation of an active subscription.

### Business Impact

• Updates subscription lifecycle

• Schedules feature expiration

---

# AIRequestSubmitted

## Purpose

Represents submission of an AI reasoning request.

Examples:

- Trade evaluation

- Player evaluation

- Team strategy

- Cap analysis

### Business Impact

• Creates AI request record

• Associates request with conversation

• Does not modify League state

---

# AIResponseReceived

## Purpose

Represents successful completion of AI reasoning.

### Business Impact

• Stores response

• Associates explanation with deterministic evidence

• Enables conversation continuity

### AI Interpretation

The AI response is advisory.

It never becomes authoritative League state.

---

# AIResponseRejected

## Purpose

Represents rejection of an AI response due to validation failure.

Examples:

- Unsupported recommendation

- Hallucinated player

- Rule violation

- Missing evidence

### Business Impact

• Discards invalid response

• Preserves deterministic reasoning

• Records validation outcome

---

# WebhookReceived

## Purpose

Represents receipt of an external webhook.

Examples:

- Payment provider

- Authentication provider

- Fantasy platform

### Business Impact

• Creates webhook record

• Begins validation

---

# WebhookProcessed

## Purpose

Represents successful processing of a webhook.

### Business Impact

• Produces Business Events where appropriate

• Updates integration history

---

# WebhookRejected

## Purpose

Represents rejection of an invalid webhook.

### Business Impact

• Preserves League integrity

• Records rejection reason

