# Relationship to Other Chapters

Integration Events never replace Business Events.

Instead they initiate, observe, or communicate them.

Examples include:

```text
ExternalDataReceived

↓

Command

↓

RosterAssignmentCreated

↓

ContractCreated

↓

AuditEventRecorded
```

The Business Events remain authoritative.

The Integration Events merely facilitate communication between Legacy and external systems.

---

# AI Interpretation

Integration Events provide authoritative evidence regarding:

- Synchronization history

- Provider health

- Authentication status

- Notification delivery

- Subscription lifecycle

- AI request history

- External system reliability

The AI shall never infer League state directly from external provider responses.

Only validated Business Events constitute deterministic League truth.

---

# Validation Checklist

Before publishing Integration Events verify:

✓ Provider authenticated

✓ Message integrity verified

✓ Validation completed

✓ Idempotency preserved

✓ Business Events emitted correctly

✓ Failures isolated

✓ Audit history preserved

✓ Retries deterministic

✓ External payload archived

✓ League state protected

---

# Final Principle

Legacy is the system of record.

External systems exchange information.

Business Events define League state.

Transactions coordinate change.

Audit Events preserve history.

Integration Events connect Legacy to the outside world without compromising deterministic reasoning or event-sourced integrity.

Every League can therefore be reconstructed entirely from Business Events, even if every external provider disappears tomorrow.
